WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:05.380
HBO might be best known for producing hit
series like The Sopranos, Westworld, and Game

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.860
of Thrones, but the pay cable network has
consistently churned out quality television

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.249
series far beyond its most popular programs.

00:00:13.249 --> 00:00:17.410
Some of its finest works have been forgotten
by time, even though many of them still hold

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:18.410
up.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.849
If you're looking for another old show stream
to fill the void until all those dragons and

00:00:21.849 --> 00:00:26.570
theme park hosts are back in action again,
here are some of the hidden HBO gems you should

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:28.339
take a look at.

00:00:28.339 --> 00:00:29.800
Angels in America

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:35.580
When it debuted back in 2003, Angels in America
was a unique television experience, and it

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:36.580
still is.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:40.980
The six-part miniseries was adapted from the
two-part play by Tony Kushner and tells the

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.400
story of the AIDS crisis through a magical
realist lens.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.690
The miniseries centers on a gay man whose
partner abandons him after he's diagnosed

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:49.690
with AIDS.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:53.690
As if that weren't enough of a burden, he's
also visited by an Angel who declares him

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:54.690
a prophet.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:01:00.170
The series features an all-star cast that
includes Justin Kirk, Ben Shenkman, Mary-Louise

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:05.930
Parker, Emma Thompson, Al Pacino, Patrick
Wilson, Jeffrey Wright, and Meryl Streep in

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:09.950
multiple roles, including a brief stint as
a male rabbi.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:11.310
Bored to Death

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:16.620
There's nothing else quite like Bored to Death,
a comedy that began in 2009 and ran for three

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:17.620
seasons.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:21.530
It stars Jason Schwartzman as a writer who
decides to distract himself from the daunting

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:25.320
prospect of his next novel by becoming an
unlicensed private detective.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:30.280
Zach Galifianakis plays his best friend, a
comic book artist, and Ted Danson appears

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:34.890
as an older friend and mentor who edits an
acclaimed magazine where Jonathan writes.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:42.120
"Oh my God, I have completely failed at the
most important thing in life."

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.890
Jonathan doesn't take his detective work all
that seriously, having learned everything

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:50.100
he knows from Raymond Chandler novels, but
as the series goes on, he gets involved in

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.710
some surprisingly dire situations.

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:57.580
This show isn't for everybody, but if you're
a mystery fan or enjoy comedies about overeducated

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:00.659
stoners failing at things, it might be for
you.

00:02:00.659 --> 00:02:01.659
Carnivàle

00:02:01.659 --> 00:02:07.840
HBO is known for its ambitious original programming,
and Carnivàle is a show that aimed incredibly

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.889
high, but never got fully off the ground.

00:02:09.889 --> 00:02:14.510
However, that doesn't mean it's not an interesting
oddity worth a watch, especially for fans

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:15.849
of dark fantasy.

00:02:15.849 --> 00:02:21.099
Set in the Dust Bowl of the mid-1930s, Carnivàle
is about a traveling carnival, but it's also

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:24.720
about a supernatural battle between destined
avatars of good and evil.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:30.709
When the series started in 2003, creator Daniel
Knauf intended it to tell one complex story

00:02:30.709 --> 00:02:32.849
over the course of six seasons.

00:02:32.849 --> 00:02:38.019
Unfortunately, HBO only ended up giving it
two, so most of that story remains untold.

00:02:38.019 --> 00:02:39.980
The Comeback

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:44.239
This Lisa Kudrow comedy ran for just two seasons
but spanned nine years.

00:02:44.239 --> 00:02:48.859
The former Friends star stars as a shallow
and self-centered '90s sitcom star trying

00:02:48.859 --> 00:02:53.189
to make a return to the fame game with a new
sitcom and a reality show.

00:02:53.189 --> 00:02:57.889
Unlike Phoebe Buffay, Kudrow's new character
is obsessed with her own image, but constantly

00:02:57.889 --> 00:02:59.730
fails to make a good impression.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:04.790
Despite her unlikability, the series also
effectively satirizes the sexist and ageist

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:09.280
entertainment industry, which has little room
and even less respect for a middle-aged sitcom

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:10.280
actress.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:14.450
The Comeback was initially canceled after
its first season in 2005, but in the years

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:17.099
to come its reputation grew.

00:03:17.099 --> 00:03:20.379
In 2014, the show was unexpectedly revived
for a second season.

00:03:20.379 --> 00:03:24.980
"Still no pages, so I thought I'd just stay
up here, stay cool, you know, thinking about

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:25.980
production."

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:29.949
The Comeback was an insightful and biting
satire from the start, but the long arc enabled

00:03:29.949 --> 00:03:34.099
by such an unusual break between seasons makes
it something truly special.

00:03:34.099 --> 00:03:38.279
We can only hope it returns for a third season
in 2023.

00:03:38.279 --> 00:03:39.569
Five Days

00:03:39.569 --> 00:03:44.870
This 2007 co-production with the BBC is a
mystery series that also serves as an effective

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.189
emotional drama.

00:03:46.189 --> 00:03:50.669
Each of the five episodes tells the story
of one day in the investigation of the mysterious

00:03:50.669 --> 00:03:54.900
disappearance of a young mother and her two
children, spanning from the very first day

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.730
to the 79th day of the search for truth.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:02.340
This method not only allows the audience to
see how much changes as the days, weeks, and

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:08.449
months roll on, but it also introduces a riveting
performance by future Selma star David Oyelowo,

00:04:08.449 --> 00:04:11.839
who appears as the father whose family vanishes.

00:04:11.839 --> 00:04:13.449
Parade's End

00:04:13.449 --> 00:04:17.479
Benedict Cumberbatch fans will definitely
want to check out Parade's End, which centers

00:04:17.479 --> 00:04:22.280
on three people whose lives in Britain are
upended by World War I. Opposite Rebecca Hall

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:27.160
and Adelaide Clemens, Cumberbatch plays a
rich conservative statistician who is badly

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.650
injured in the war.

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:33.440
The entire five-episode miniseries was written
by acclaimed playwright Tom Stoppard and directed

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:38.180
by Susanna White, and serves as a formidable
British period drama.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:39.520
Togetherness

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:44.560
Titans of indie filmmaking, brothers Mark
and Jay Duplass collaborated with Steve Zissis

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:49.500
to create the pilot for Togetherness, which
premiered in 2015 and ran for two seasons.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:54.810
Mark Duplass plays Brett Pierson, a Los Angeles
sound editor with a wife and two kids.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:59.250
Melanie Lynskey plays his wife Michelle, who's
concerned about their romantic life.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:03.870
Amanda Peet is Tina Morris, Michelle's sister
who unexpectedly moves in with their family

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.319
after splitting up with her boyfriend in Houston.

00:05:06.319 --> 00:05:11.340
Zissis appears as Alex, Brett's best friend,
who also moves in when his acting career isn't

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:12.340
going well.

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:16.360
As anyone who's watched a television show
could guess, an attraction develops between

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:21.220
Tina and Alex which gets increasingly complicated
as the show goes on.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:24.639
In other ways, starting with the Duplass brothers'
dialogue, the show is quite unlike the usual

00:05:24.639 --> 00:05:28.150
TV comedies, and its two seasons are well
worth a look.

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:29.860
Thanks for watching!

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:32.750
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:34.990
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

